WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.383
Look at all the buildings here.

00:00:02.383 --> 00:00:05.416
They are covered with television screens.

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:07.866
Where are we?

00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:09.100
Oh!

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.200
This is Times Square

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.066
and we must be in...

00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:15.533
New York City.

00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:45.600
This is a major city in America.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.266
It has the largest population of any city in the United States.

00:00:51.266 --> 00:00:54.566
Over 8 million people!

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:58.616
That's a lot of people.

00:00:58.616 --> 00:01:03.116
Over 800 different languages are spoken here.

00:01:03.116 --> 00:01:08.016
More than any other city or place in the world.

00:01:08.016 --> 00:01:10.916
New York City has been given

00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:14.333
many different nicknames over the years.

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:16.700
The most well-known being

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.166
the 'Big Apple'.

00:01:20.216 --> 00:01:25.016
The city is split into five different areas.

00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:28.700
These areas are known as boroughs.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.533
These boroughs are called

00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:33.750
Queens,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.633
The Bronx,

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:37.616
Staten Island,

00:01:37.616 --> 00:01:38.516
Brooklyn

00:01:38.516 --> 00:01:39.783
and...

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.733
Manhattan.

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:44.233
Because New York City has been built

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.866
across several different islands.

00:01:46.866 --> 00:01:52.266
Many of the boroughs of the city are separated by water.

00:01:52.266 --> 00:01:54.466
Speaking of water...

00:01:54.466 --> 00:01:56.166
what's out there

00:01:56.166 --> 00:01:59.150
in the middle of New York Harbor?

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.100
Oh!

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.266
That's the Statue of Liberty.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:07.633
The Statue of Liberty was a present from France.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:13.033
It was given to America to celebrate the end of slavery

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:16.066
after the civil war.

00:02:16.066 --> 00:02:20.283
The statue took four months to build

00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:26.416
and it's now one of the most iconic sights in New York City.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.883
The island that the statue sits on is called

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.500
Liberty Island.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.933
It's a popular tourist attraction.

00:02:36.933 --> 00:02:39.816
You can go inside the statue

00:02:39.816 --> 00:02:44.650
and walk all the way up into the crown.

00:02:47.216 --> 00:02:48.300
Did you know

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:54.816
that the Statue of Liberty wears a size 879 shoe?

00:02:54.816 --> 00:02:57.483
Those are some big shoes.

00:02:57.483 --> 00:03:02.216
Luckily it hasn't needed another pair yet.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.333
The statue is green today.

00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:09.900
But when it was first built, it was brown.

00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:13.250
That's because it's made out of copper

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.166
which when left out in the air for a long time,

00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:17.066
turns green.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.033
Look over there.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.166
There's a boat!

00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:25.100
Oh!

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:29.116
That's the Staten Island Ferry.

00:03:29.116 --> 00:03:32.050
This is a free to ride boat.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:37.750
That travels from Manhattan to Staten Island.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.283
Let's get on.

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.750
Where are we now?

00:03:46.916 --> 00:03:47.833
Oh!

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.583
We're back in Times Square

00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:52.050
in Manhattan.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:55.083
Look at all these billboards

00:03:55.083 --> 00:04:00.666
lighting up the night sky.

00:04:00.666 --> 00:04:03.016
There are lots of people here,

00:04:03.016 --> 00:04:05.233
all rushing around.

00:04:05.233 --> 00:04:10.633
This is a very busy part of New York City.

00:04:11.816 --> 00:04:16.316
Times Square is known as the center of entertainment

00:04:16.366 --> 00:04:18.866
in New York City.

00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:22.350
Visitors can go sightseeing

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.600
or see a show

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.500
at the famous theater district of broadway.

00:04:28.416 --> 00:04:34.050
The Square has always been a very popular place for tourists

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.283
all throughout its history.

00:04:37.783 --> 00:04:43.433
A long time ago, this area was called Longacre Square.

00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:47.266
The name was later changed to Times Square

00:04:47.266 --> 00:04:50.466
when the newspaper, the New York Times

00:04:50.466 --> 00:04:55.550
built its headquarters here.

00:04:56.266 --> 00:04:58.600
Let's go somewhere new.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.066
Taxi!

00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:04.150
Let's get a yellow taxi cab.

00:05:04.933 --> 00:05:10.283
New York City is well-known for its taxis.

00:05:10.283 --> 00:05:14.633
They can be found almost anywhere in the city.

00:05:14.633 --> 00:05:17.783
They are a great way to get around

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:21.483
if there's not too much traffic.

00:05:21.483 --> 00:05:26.650
The only problem is getting one to stop and give you a lift!

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.133
Taxi!

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.200
Wow.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.750
Look at all the trees.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.450
Are we still in the city?

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:41.766
Yes!

00:05:42.466 --> 00:05:44.366
This is Central Park.

00:05:52.766 --> 00:05:58.516
This is a large urban park in the center of Manhattan.

00:06:00.516 --> 00:06:06.266
Central Park is the most filmed location in the world.

00:06:09.483 --> 00:06:12.983
You've probably seen it in a movie.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:22.400
While most people come to enjoy the peaceful surroundings.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.200
The park also contains

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.716
a carousel,

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.616
Belvedere Castle,

00:06:36.583 --> 00:06:38.550
The Central Park Zoo,

00:06:42.216 --> 00:06:46.316
and the Bethesda Terrace.

00:06:48.166 --> 00:06:50.833
If you don't want to walk,

00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:55.366
you can go on a horse and carriage ride.

00:06:55.833 --> 00:07:02.750
These rides will take you all around the park.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:07.116
Let's get back into a taxi.

00:07:09.583 --> 00:07:11.850
Where are we now?

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.316
We are driving over a big bridge.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.633
This is the Brooklyn Bridge.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.383
The Brooklyn Bridge connects the boroughs

00:07:28.383 --> 00:07:31.383
of Manhattan and Brooklyn.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.616
See those cables, holding up the base of the bridge?

00:07:38.616 --> 00:07:42.383
This design makes it a suspension bridge.

00:07:42.816 --> 00:07:45.700
When the bridge was first opened,

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:50.500
it was the longest suspension bridge in the world.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.966
It no longer holds this title.

00:07:53.966 --> 00:07:59.633
However, as you can see, it's still an impressive bridge

00:07:59.633 --> 00:08:04.166
and has inspired many artists and photographers

00:08:04.166 --> 00:08:06.550
over the years.

00:08:07.933 --> 00:08:10.600
Let's follow these people.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.800
Where are they going?

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.383
Oh!

00:08:14.383 --> 00:08:17.616
They're going on the subway.

00:08:18.216 --> 00:08:21.483
The New York Subway is the busiest

00:08:21.483 --> 00:08:25.566
underground train system in the world.

00:08:25.566 --> 00:08:31.716
Nearly 3 million people use the subway every day.

00:08:31.716 --> 00:08:36.716
Let's get on a train and go somewhere new.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.483
We are back in Manhattan.

00:08:42.483 --> 00:08:43.466
Look up!

00:08:43.466 --> 00:08:47.783
What's that tall building?

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:54.166
That's the Empire State Building.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:57.700
This building is a famous skyscraper

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.083
on the New York City skyline.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.366
It is built in the style known as Art Deco.

00:09:06.366 --> 00:09:10.750
The building has 102 floors.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.483
Most of the floors contain offices.

00:09:14.483 --> 00:09:18.900
But the building is open to tourists too.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:24.050
Visitors can go all the way to the top of the skyscraper.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:28.083
At the top, there is a viewing platform.

00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:31.616
From the viewing platform you can see

00:09:31.616 --> 00:09:35.600
across the Midtown area of Manhattan.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:41.166
Be careful it can get windy at the top!

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:48.616
The Empire State Building was made famous

00:09:48.616 --> 00:09:53.816
worldwide by the classic movie 'King Kong'.

00:09:55.316 --> 00:09:59.133
At the end of the movie, King Kong climbs

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:02.250
all the way to the top of the building.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.150
But I don't want to say any more about the film

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.833
as I don't want to spoil the ending.

00:10:08.766 --> 00:10:12.650
There are other famous skyscrapers in New York City,

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.116
such as,

00:10:14.116 --> 00:10:17.183
the Flatiron Building

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:19.883
known for its unusual triangle shape.

00:10:20.716 --> 00:10:22.483
The Woolworth Building,

00:10:22.483 --> 00:10:27.650
one of the oldest skyscrapers in the city.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.600
And the Chrysler Building.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.450
Like the Empire State Building,

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:39.083
the Chrysler Building was also built in the Art Deco style.

00:10:39.083 --> 00:10:45.883
At the time, it was a rival to the Empire State Building.

00:10:51.916 --> 00:10:53.266
What's that?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:57.833
Oh, it's my stomach rumbling.

00:10:57.833 --> 00:10:59.666
I must be hungry.

00:11:00.116 --> 00:11:03.833
Let's stop for something to eat.

00:11:03.833 --> 00:11:06.300
But what should we have?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.500
I know let's have a pizza.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:15.450
New York City is famous for its pizza.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:20.000
Italian immigrants brought pizza to New York City

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.833
over a hundred years ago,

00:11:22.833 --> 00:11:27.383
and it has been a popular dish ever since.

00:11:27.383 --> 00:11:32.433
New York style is a large slice of pizza that can be folded

00:11:32.433 --> 00:11:37.333
with tomato sauce and mozzarella cheese.

00:11:37.333 --> 00:11:38.350
Hmm.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:41.316
That looks delicious.

00:11:41.316 --> 00:11:46.533
Let's take a walk and work off that pizza.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:53.200
Where are we now?

00:11:56.216 --> 00:12:00.600
This is Wall Street.

00:12:01.333 --> 00:12:07.583
Wall Street is in the financial district of Lower Manhattan.

00:12:07.766 --> 00:12:11.783
Two large stock exchanges are based here

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:15.550
and several banking headquarters.

00:12:16.016 --> 00:12:19.100
There's a statue of a bull here too

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:22.583
known as the 'Charging Bull'.

00:12:22.583 --> 00:12:28.566
The bull symbolizes healthy market conditions.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:32.600
Let's keep on walking.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.616
This building looks brand new.

00:12:37.616 --> 00:12:38.500
Oh!

00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:42.450
It's One World Trade Center.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:49.533
This is the main building of the rebuilt World Trade Center,

00:12:49.533 --> 00:12:55.416
which was destroyed in the September 11th attacks.

00:12:55.416 --> 00:13:00.766
This is now the tallest building in the United States,

00:13:00.766 --> 00:13:06.483
taller than the towers that stood there before.

00:13:08.716 --> 00:13:12.250
The building shows the world that New York

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.250
will always rebuild itself,

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.866
even after tragedy.

00:13:18.816 --> 00:13:24.250
On the site, there is also a museum and a memorial

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:30.183
that pays respect to those who lost their lives.

00:13:31.283 --> 00:13:35.016
Let's get back on the subway.

00:13:35.266 --> 00:13:37.250
Where are we now?

00:13:37.266 --> 00:13:41.400
This is a building in a part of New York City

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.900
called Greenwich Village.

00:13:44.083 --> 00:13:48.350
It doesn't look that special, does it?

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.333
Hmm.

00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:52.566
But maybe it does look familiar to you.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.433
That's because it was used in the

00:13:55.433 --> 00:13:59.600
popular television series, Friends.

00:13:59.816 --> 00:14:03.783
Even though the series ended many years ago,

00:14:03.783 --> 00:14:06.533
it's still very popular.

00:14:06.533 --> 00:14:12.333
People come from all over the world to see this building.

00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:16.966
Does anyone want to grab a coffee at Central Perk?

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:21.516
Taxi!

00:14:23.583 --> 00:14:26.050
What's going on here?

00:14:26.316 --> 00:14:29.866
There are loads of balloons everywhere.

00:14:31.116 --> 00:14:36.883
Oh, this is the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:14:38.533 --> 00:14:42.516
This is the world's largest parade.

00:14:45.366 --> 00:14:48.216
People come out into the streets to see

00:14:48.216 --> 00:14:51.883
the balloons, floats and marching bands

00:14:51.883 --> 00:14:55.516
parading through Manhattan.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.850
Many well-known characters are turned into balloons,

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:03.900
which can be seen high above the crowds.

00:15:04.966 --> 00:15:07.916
It's very impressive.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:10.650
Whoa.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.450
Look at that balloon,

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.266
it's huge!

00:15:15.066 --> 00:15:20.400
The first Macy's Day Parade happened back in 1924.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.316
It was created by the US-based

00:15:23.316 --> 00:15:27.416
department-store chain, Macy's.

00:15:29.166 --> 00:15:31.866
Let's head back to the subway.

00:15:31.866 --> 00:15:35.166
How about we go watch some sports?

00:15:40.916 --> 00:15:41.766
Oh!

00:15:41.766 --> 00:15:44.666
Look at this building!

00:15:44.666 --> 00:15:49.583
This is the New York Yankees home stadium.

00:15:49.583 --> 00:15:54.400
The New York Yankees are a professional baseball team.

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:58.583
Baseball is a popular sport in New York 

00:15:58.583 --> 00:16:02.533
and the United States.

00:16:04.116 --> 00:16:08.050
The Yankees are considered to be one of the greatest

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:13.750
and most successful teams in the history of the sport.

00:16:13.866 --> 00:16:16.900
Let's get a hot dog and enjoy the game.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:20.316
Give me lots of onion and mustard!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.816
I hope you enjoyed your time in New York City.

00:16:25.816 --> 00:16:28.716
If you enjoyed this video.

00:16:28.716 --> 00:16:31.450
Don't forget to like, and subscribe.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.500
Thank you for watching this SimpleEnglish Video.

00:16:40.866 --> 00:16:43.300
